467	7fcb83a5-3b9d-42d9-a94a-be60eed68f20	uk	{"display_title": "Тестовий документ", "markdown_body": "# Kami Documentation Markdown Test\\r\\n\\r\\nThis file is intended as a small rendering test for Markdown parsers used by Kami documentation.\\r\\n\\r\\nIt contains common documentation elements, several code blocks, tables, links, lists, quotes, and a few edge cases.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. Basic formatting\\r\\n\\r\\nRegular paragraph with **bold text**, *italic text*, ~~strikethrough~~, and `inline code`.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can also combine formatting, for example: **important `Request` behavior** or *optional `display_order` value*.\\r\\n\\r\\nUseful links:\\r\\n\\r\\n- [KamiCore](https://kamicore.org/)\\r\\n- [CommonMark](https://commonmark.org/)\\r\\n- [PostgreSQL documentation](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/)\\r\\n\\r\\nA raw URL may also be useful in documentation:\\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://kamicore.org/\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. Headings and anchors\\r\\n\\r\\n### Request lifecycle\\r\\n\\r\\nA typical request may pass through several stages:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Parse the URL.\\r\\n2. Resolve the current page.\\r\\n3. Initialize plugins.\\r\\n4. Let a plugin accept a routed item.\\r\\n5. Render plugin output.\\r\\n6. Finalize the page.\\r\\n7. Send the response.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Notes\\r\\n\\r\\n> Documentation should explain current behavior rather than historical implementation details.\\r\\n\\r\\n> **Note:** Markdown is the source format. Rendered HTML is only a presentation layer.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 3. Configuration table\\r\\n\\r\\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\\r\\n|---|---|---:|---|\\r\\n| `enabled` | boolean | `true` | Enables the feature. |\\r\\n| `items_per_page` | integer | `20` | Number of items displayed on one page. |\\r\\n| `template` | string | `default` | Template used for rendering. |\\r\\n| `show_pagination` | boolean | `true` | Displays pagination controls. |\\r\\n| `display_order` | integer | `0` | Controls ordering inside the parent node. |\\r\\n\\r\\n### Field storage example\\r\\n\\r\\n| Field type | PostgreSQL storage | Translatable | Typical use |\\r\\n|---|---|---|---|\\r\\n| `text` | `item_texts` | yes/no | Titles, names, short text |\\r\\n| `number` | `item_numbers` | no | Prices, counters, numeric values |\\r\\n| `date` | `item_dates` | no | Publication and event dates |\\r\\n| `markdown` | text / JSONB source | yes | Documentation, long-form technical text |\\r\\n| `compound` | JSONB / structured values | yes/no | Repeated structured components |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 4. PHP example\\r\\n\\r\\n```php\\r\\n<?php\\r\\n\\r\\n$result = pg_query_params(\\r\\n    $db,\\r\\n    'SELECT doc_id, title, raw_text\\r\\n     FROM documentation\\r\\n     WHERE parent_id IS NOT DISTINCT FROM $1\\r\\n     ORDER BY display_order, title',\\r\\n    [$parentId]\\r\\n);\\r\\n\\r\\nif ($result === false) {\\r\\n    throw new RuntimeException('Unable to load documentation nodes.');\\r\\n}\\r\\n\\r\\nwhile ($row = pg_fetch_assoc($result)) {\\r\\n    echo $row['title'] . PHP_EOL;\\r\\n}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nA shorter PHP fragment:\\r\\n\\r\\n```php\\r\\n$hash = hash('sha256', $markdown);\\r\\n\\r\\nif ($hash !== $storedHash) {\\r\\n    updateDocumentation($docId, $markdown, $hash);\\r\\n}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 5. JavaScript example\\r\\n\\r\\n```js\\r\\ndocument.addEventListener('click', async (event) => {\\r\\n    const button = event.target.closest('[data-doc-preview]');\\r\\n\\r\\n    if (!button) {\\r\\n        return;\\r\\n    }\\r\\n\\r\\n    const response = await fetch('/ajax/ViewMd/preview', {\\r\\n        method: 'POST',\\r\\n        headers: {\\r\\n            'Content-Type': 'application/json'\\r\\n        },\\r\\n        body: JSON.stringify({\\r\\n            markdown: document.querySelector('#raw_text').value\\r\\n        })\\r\\n    });\\r\\n\\r\\n    const data = await response.json();\\r\\n\\r\\n    document.querySelector('#preview').innerHTML = data.html;\\r\\n});\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 6. JSON example\\r\\n\\r\\n```json\\r\\n{\\r\\n    \\"name\\": \\"ViewMd\\",\\r\\n    \\"version\\": \\"0.1.0\\",\\r\\n    \\"description\\": \\"Renders Markdown content as HTML\\",\\r\\n    \\"settings\\": {\\r\\n        \\"safe_mode\\": true,\\r\\n        \\"breaks_enabled\\": false\\r\\n    }\\r\\n}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 7. HTML example\\r\\n\\r\\n```html\\r\\n<article class=\\"documentation-page\\">\\r\\n    <header>\\r\\n        <h1>Rendering Markdown</h1>\\r\\n    </header>\\r\\n\\r\\n    <div class=\\"documentation-content\\">\\r\\n        <!-- Rendered Markdown is inserted here -->\\r\\n    </div>\\r\\n</article>\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 8. Nested lists\\r\\n\\r\\n- Core\\r\\n  - Request\\r\\n    - URL parsing\\r\\n    - Path parameters\\r\\n    - Routed items\\r\\n  - Response\\r\\n    - Status codes\\r\\n    - Headers\\r\\n- Plugins\\r\\n  - Lifecycle\\r\\n  - ACL\\r\\n  - AJAX\\r\\n  - API\\r\\n- Themes\\r\\n  - Layouts\\r\\n  - Templates\\r\\n  - Assets\\r\\n\\r\\nNumbered variant:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Install the plugin.\\r\\n2. Enable it.\\r\\n3. Create a Markdown field.\\r\\n   1. Add the field definition.\\r\\n   2. Assign it to a content type.\\r\\n   3. Save the structure.\\r\\n4. Render the field with `ViewMd`.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 9. Task list\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] Store Markdown as raw text.\\r\\n- [x] Render Markdown only for output.\\r\\n- [x] Keep HTML out of the source content.\\r\\n- [ ] Add documentation search.\\r\\n- [ ] Add documentation versioning.\\r\\n- [ ] Add source file synchronization.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 10. Definition-style section\\r\\n\\r\\n### `source_file`\\r\\n\\r\\nOptional path to a Markdown source file.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf it is set, the file may be treated as the canonical source and the database record as the searchable site representation.\\r\\n\\r\\n### `raw_text`\\r\\n\\r\\nThe original Markdown content.\\r\\n\\r\\nIt should not contain cached HTML.\\r\\n\\r\\n### `display_order`\\r\\n\\r\\nControls the position of the document among sibling nodes.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 11. Command-line examples\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\nphp install.php\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\ngit checkout alpha-0.5\\r\\ngit pull\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n```sql\\r\\nSELECT\\r\\n    doc_id,\\r\\n    parent_id,\\r\\n    title,\\r\\n    source_file,\\r\\n    display_order\\r\\nFROM documentation\\r\\nORDER BY parent_id NULLS FIRST, display_order, title;\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 12. Escaping and special characters\\r\\n\\r\\nMarkdown should handle symbols such as:\\r\\n\\r\\n- `&`\\r\\n- `<`\\r\\n- `>`\\r\\n- `\\"quoted text\\"`\\r\\n- `'single quotes'`\\r\\n- `{placeholder}`\\r\\n- `/path/value`\\r\\n- `foo_bar`\\r\\n- `some-value`\\r\\n\\r\\nEscaped Markdown characters:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\\\*not italic\\\\*\\r\\n\\r\\n\\\\# not a heading\\r\\n\\r\\n\\\\`not inline code\\\\`\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 13. Long code line\\r\\n\\r\\nThis section is useful for checking horizontal scrolling inside `<pre>` blocks.\\r\\n\\r\\n```php\\r\\n$documentationUrl = $baseUrl . '/documentation/' . $language . '/' . $sectionSlug . '/' . $documentSlug . '?preview=1&source=database';\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 14. Blockquote with code\\r\\n\\r\\n> A routed item should only be accepted by a plugin that can actually render it.\\r\\n>\\r\\n> Example:\\r\\n>\\r\\n> ```php\\r\\n> if (!$this->supports($item)) {\\r\\n>     $this->declineRoutedItem();\\r\\n> }\\r\\n> ```\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 15. Horizontal rules\\r\\n\\r\\nThe following sections are separated by horizontal rules.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\nFirst section.\\r\\n\\r\\n***\\r\\n\\r\\nSecond section.\\r\\n\\r\\n___\\r\\n\\r\\nThird section.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 16. Image syntax\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is intentionally remote and may be replaced during testing:\\r\\n\\r\\n![Example documentation image](https://kamicore.org/favicon.ico)\\r\\n\\r\\nImage with title:\\r\\n\\r\\n![Kami example](https://kamicore.org/favicon.ico \\"Kami\\")\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 17. Inline HTML test\\r\\n\\r\\nThis block is useful for checking safe mode behavior:\\r\\n\\r\\n<div class=\\"should-be-filtered-or-escaped\\">\\r\\n    Raw HTML block.\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n\\r\\nAnd an inline fragment: <strong>raw HTML strong tag</strong>.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 18. Potentially unsafe links\\r\\n\\r\\nThese are useful for checking URL sanitization:\\r\\n\\r\\n[Normal HTTPS link](https://example.com/)\\r\\n\\r\\n[Mail link](mailto:test@example.com)\\r\\n\\r\\n[Unsafe JavaScript link](javascript:alert('test'))\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 19. Mixed documentation example\\r\\n\\r\\n### Saving documentation\\r\\n\\r\\nThe source text is stored in `raw_text`.\\r\\n\\r\\n```php\\r\\n$sql = <<<'SQL'\\r\\n    UPDATE documentation\\r\\n    SET raw_text = $1,\\r\\n        source_hash = $2,\\r\\n        updated_at = NOW()\\r\\n    WHERE doc_id = $3\\r\\nSQL;\\r\\n\\r\\n$result = pg_query_params($db, $sql, [\\r\\n    $markdown,\\r\\n    hash('sha256', $markdown),\\r\\n    $docId,\\r\\n]);\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter saving:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. invalidate the rendered cache;\\r\\n2. update the search vector if needed;\\r\\n3. keep `source_file` unchanged;\\r\\n4. do not store generated HTML in the main record.\\r\\n\\r\\n> **Important:** The database may contain both file-backed and database-only documentation pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## 20. Final parser checks\\r\\n\\r\\nSome compact syntax combinations:\\r\\n\\r\\n`inline_code()` next to **bold text**.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Bold with [a link](https://example.com/).**\\r\\n\\r\\n*Italic with `inline code`.*\\r\\n\\r\\nA paragraph  \\r\\nwith a manual line break.\\r\\n\\r\\nA paragraph\\r\\nwith a normal line break in the Markdown source.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\nEnd of test file.\\r\\n"}	draft	f	2026-09-13 13:31:07.762074+00
